  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mongolia: Strengthening Child Rights in Mongolia Through Digital Literacy and Legal Empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To enhance Mongolian children and adolescents&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; media literacy, critical thinking, and responsible digital engagement. 2) To enable Mongolian adolescents to effectively exercise, advocate for, and claim their rights under the Convention on the Rights of the Child and its third Optional Protocol.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Children, adolescents, caregivers, teachers and educators, Governmental child protection institutions, child protection civil society organizations, youth and women-led organizations.Indirect beneficiaries: Population at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the child protection framework in Mongolia by equipping children with the skills to navigate digital environments safely and empowering them to actively safeguard and claim their rights.</narrative>
  </description>
